  "summary_en": "Deliverable D1.2 of the EU Horizon 2020 MARIO project: a multi-layered ethical framework for care robots serving older people with dementia. It reviews roboethics literature and prior projects, analyses care integration, quality of care, functionalities and design/data issues, then applies them to MARIO use cases, with informed-consent guidance.",
  "title_clean": "D1.2 Ethics Framework: Managing active and healthy aging with use of caring service robots",
  "title_en": "D1.2 Ethics Framework: Managing active and healthy aging with use of caring service robots",
  "venue": "MARIO Project (Horizon 2020) deliverable; University of Twente repository",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Four-layer ethical framework: care process integration, quality of care, robot functionalities, design and ICT capabilities",
   "Care robots are double-edged, with both ethical risks and improvements",
   "Emphasises privacy, data protection and dynamic informed consent for vulnerable participants with dementia",
   "Draws on care ethics, value sensitive design and capability approach",
   "Applies the framework to MARIO use-case scenarios and notes lack of standards for non-factory robots"
